# Copy relevant values into your own untracked local configuration.
# Never commit real secrets. This file documents which values exist —
# it does not itself contain any.

# --- EF Core CLI (design-time only) ---------------------------------------
# Used by Prime.Infrastructure/Persistence/PrimeDbContextFactory.cs when
# running `dotnet ef migrations add` / `dotnet ef database update` from the
# command line, outside the WebApi host.
# Local dev: point at the local PostgreSQL 16 install.
# Supabase environments: use the DIRECT (port 5432) connection string, not
# the pooled one — see docs/DATABASE.md §1.1.
PRIME_DB_CONNECTION=Host=localhost;Port=5432;Database=prime_dev;Username=postgres;Password=

# --- Prime.WebApi runtime configuration -----------------------------------
# ASP.NET Core reads double-underscore env vars as nested config, e.g.
# ConnectionStrings__PrimeDb maps to configuration["ConnectionStrings:PrimeDb"].
# Local dev values normally live in src/Prime.WebApi/appsettings.Development.json
# (gitignored) instead of real environment variables; this file documents
# both paths for staging/production, where env vars are the actual mechanism.

# Local dev: local Postgres. Staging/prod: Supabase's POOLED (port 6543)
# connection string, with Max Auto Prepare=0 (see docs/DATABASE.md §1.1).
ConnectionStrings__PrimeDb=

# Supabase project base URL, e.g. https://xxxxxxxx.supabase.co
# That's all Prime.WebApi needs for JWT validation — this project uses
# Supabase's newer JWT Signing Keys (asymmetric, ES256), so Prime.WebApi
# validates via standard OIDC discovery at {Supabase__Url}/auth/v1/
# .well-known/openid-configuration and fetches/rotates signing keys
# automatically. There is no shared secret to configure. (If a future
# Supabase project instead uses the legacy shared JWT secret, this
# approach would need to change — check Settings > API > JWT Settings
# before assuming.)
Supabase__Url=

# Supabase service role key — bypasses RLS. Server-side only, never sent to
# the frontend, never logged. Required once Storage signed-URL generation
# (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §3.9) is implemented (Phase 4+).
Supabase__ServiceRoleKey=

# Frontend origin(s) allowed to call the API via CORS.
Cors__AllowedOrigins__0=http://localhost:5173

# --- frontend/prime-web (Vite) ---------------------------------------------
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_ to client code. The anon key is
# safe for the frontend (it is meant to be public — RLS enforces access, not
# secrecy of this key). The service role key must NEVER appear here.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://localhost:7221
